WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
This show contains scenes that some viewers may 
find disturbing. Viewer discretion is advised.

00:09.910 --> 00:14.120
Sword Prince, to those who see what should 
be seen and speak what should be spoken,

00:14.120 --> 00:15.490
grant your protection!

00:22.660 --> 00:24.460
Everyone, please heal!

00:25.400 --> 00:28.630
First, we need to silence our enemy's spells.

00:28.630 --> 00:29.660
Right!

00:29.660 --> 00:30.640
We need to work together.

00:30.640 --> 00:31.830
Yes, please!

00:31.830 --> 00:37.760
My god, the roaming wind. Let all we 
say on the road stay secret among us.

00:38.060 --> 00:40.610
Let there be the light of silence.

00:40.610 --> 00:41.910
Silence!

00:52.190 --> 00:53.630
Too slow!

00:59.050 --> 01:01.540
I have no idea what you're saying!

01:22.410 --> 01:23.750
It's trying to summon more allies!

01:23.750 --> 01:26.690
We'll exterminate them all anyway. 
Perhaps we should wait until more show up.

01:27.650 --> 01:29.240
Please do this with me.

01:29.240 --> 01:30.140
Right.

01:32.050 --> 01:33.030
Ventus!

01:33.530 --> 01:34.530
Lumen!

01:36.490 --> 01:37.420
Libero!

01:49.290 --> 01:53.290
Yeah, that's about what you'd 
expect from greater demons.

01:49.690 --> 01:54.610
<b>Once There Was Youth, Now There Is Nothing but Ash</b>

01:53.290 --> 01:55.340
How far have we come?

01:55.340 --> 01:56.050
Oh, right.

01:56.330 --> 01:59.760
Two vertically and two to the side...

02:00.560 --> 02:03.930
We should be in the middle 
of the ninth floor now.

02:04.230 --> 02:05.420
Thanks.

02:08.330 --> 02:09.850
But truly...

02:10.330 --> 02:14.430
Thank goodness we haven't 
run into any goblins.

03:56.480 --> 03:57.590
Well, that sucked.

03:57.890 --> 03:59.820
Maybe I'll buy some steel arrows, too.

03:59.820 --> 04:01.970
What happened to your pride as an elf?!

04:01.970 --> 04:04.590
Just shut up and shoot! 
Shoot and distract it!

04:04.590 --> 04:06.470
You shut up and do something!

04:06.700 --> 04:08.600
I'm thinking, damn it!

04:17.060 --> 04:19.320
O merciful Earth Mother,

04:19.320 --> 04:23.650
please protect us, the weak, 
with the powers of the earth.

04:25.740 --> 04:26.700
Now!

04:26.700 --> 04:27.700
Indeed!

04:27.700 --> 04:32.000
River-Walker Mosasaurus, see my deeds!

04:43.880 --> 04:46.800
At this rate, it's gonna eventually sink!

04:53.010 --> 04:53.920
Are you a goblin?

04:53.920 --> 04:55.300
No!

04:55.300 --> 04:58.590
We were informed that a fishery 
was being attacked by sea goblins.

04:58.590 --> 05:02.250
Sea goblins?! 
At least call us Homo Piscesians.

05:02.250 --> 05:06.960
We're descendants of the great octopus god 
that cometh down from the sea of stars!

05:06.960 --> 05:09.730
We would never attack fisheries.

05:09.730 --> 05:13.660
Then do you know why there 
have been less fish lately?

05:13.660 --> 05:19.630
If it's within our power, I believe 
we can help clear your names.

05:20.090 --> 05:23.340
The reason is... the sea serpent.

05:23.340 --> 05:25.370
Sea serpent?

05:25.370 --> 05:27.760
Don't those exist further out to sea?

05:27.760 --> 05:31.150
Well, it seems they've been 
sent over here by someone.

05:31.150 --> 05:34.850
Isn't it awful? The stars have 
been a mess because of it.

05:35.090 --> 05:37.880
So... no goblins are involved?

05:38.440 --> 05:39.710
Should we go home?

05:43.530 --> 05:48.170
Then I guess we can just go ourselves. 
We can't just ignore those who are in trouble.

05:48.170 --> 05:52.080
Right. Though this seems dangerous 
with no one on our front line.

05:56.780 --> 05:57.870
What do you think?

05:57.870 --> 06:00.220
There isn't much time.

06:00.220 --> 06:02.430
What was this thing called again?

06:02.430 --> 06:04.320
A sea serpent.

06:04.320 --> 06:06.410
So is it a fish or a snake?

06:07.770 --> 06:10.570
I don't see any traces of 
venom in its bite marks.

06:10.570 --> 06:12.300
Perhaps it is a fish.

06:12.300 --> 06:16.100
Then we should just do with spells 
what we can't do with weapons.

06:22.140 --> 06:24.010
Once that thing comes out, 
let loose the spear!

06:24.010 --> 06:25.360
Yes, understood.

06:31.410 --> 06:32.380
Curse you!

06:32.380 --> 06:34.290
O merciful Earth Mother, please bless us,

06:34.290 --> 06:38.000
the wanderers in the 
darkness, with holy light!

06:45.840 --> 06:46.460
Go!

06:46.460 --> 06:48.310
You got it!

06:50.570 --> 06:52.590
Dance, dance, nymphs and sylphs!

06:52.860 --> 06:56.660
Make sure not to fall in 
between the shore and sea!

07:01.560 --> 07:02.730
Yeesh...

07:03.030 --> 07:07.250
After having the Water Walk spell 
cast on them, fish will suffocate.

07:07.700 --> 07:10.340
If it comes this way, shoot it 
with your arrows. In the eyes.

07:10.340 --> 07:11.280
Yeah, yeah.

07:24.290 --> 07:25.400
What?

07:25.920 --> 07:26.880
Nothing.

07:27.610 --> 07:30.920
I was just thinking it'd be nice if 
goblins also went down this easily.

07:34.720 --> 07:37.890
So... what happened with the quest 
to exterminate the sea goblins?

07:37.890 --> 07:39.770
They weren't goblins.

07:39.770 --> 07:42.490
Apparently, it was just 
easier to call them that.

07:42.490 --> 07:44.020
They weren't goblins.

07:44.020 --> 07:45.520
Er... So about the quest...

07:45.520 --> 07:47.200
They weren't goblins.

07:47.200 --> 07:49.800
So it's canceled. Got it.

07:49.800 --> 07:51.610
Well, they weren't goblins.

07:51.610 --> 07:53.430
So the issue with the sea goblins—

07:53.430 --> 07:57.280
Er, pardon. The issue with the 
gillmen remains unresolved.

07:57.280 --> 08:02.390
Yeah, well, we ended up exterminating 
some other creature.

08:02.390 --> 08:06.450
Oh, then can you give me the 
details on this creature?

08:06.450 --> 08:07.530
It was long.

08:07.530 --> 08:08.090
What?

08:08.510 --> 08:09.590
It was a fish.

08:09.590 --> 08:11.260
Yes... Of course.

08:12.630 --> 08:14.260
We'll now divide up our reward.

08:14.610 --> 08:18.180
Take whatever you want. We'll turn 
the rest into gold and split that.

08:18.180 --> 08:18.940
Does that work?

08:18.940 --> 08:20.440
I believe so.

08:20.440 --> 08:23.850
Those gillmen were quite generous.

08:25.260 --> 08:28.530
And this is exactly why people 
think dwarves are greedy.

08:28.530 --> 08:32.580
Oh, shut it. Of course you wouldn't 
realize the value of this, long-ears.

08:32.580 --> 08:33.700
Ain't that right, Scaly?

08:33.700 --> 08:37.660
For me, I would say this 
is the greatest reward.

08:37.660 --> 08:39.790
That's a gem, isn't it?

08:39.790 --> 08:40.690
Indeed.

08:40.690 --> 08:46.180
This is the jaw of a great dragon that 
has spent years turning into agate.

08:47.080 --> 08:49.200
Then I'll take...

08:49.200 --> 08:50.000
This!

08:50.000 --> 08:51.840
What're you gonna do with that?

08:51.840 --> 08:53.990
I figured I'd send it to my sister.

08:53.990 --> 08:56.970
Things from the sea are 
extremely rare back home.

08:56.970 --> 08:59.440
In that case, I'll take these pearls.

08:59.440 --> 09:01.760
I want to offer these to the Earth Mother.

09:01.760 --> 09:05.830
I'll be taking this helix. 
It'll work great as a catalyst.

09:05.830 --> 09:07.620
What about you, Beard-cutter?

09:07.930 --> 09:08.750
Me?

09:13.130 --> 09:14.070
I...

09:18.750 --> 09:20.370
Go on. Eat up.

09:20.370 --> 09:21.750
I have a gift for you.

09:21.750 --> 09:24.680
A gift... Wait, what? No way.

09:24.680 --> 09:25.640
I do.

09:26.890 --> 09:28.040
Found it.

09:28.040 --> 09:29.230
What is it?

09:29.620 --> 09:30.410
A seashell.

09:32.270 --> 09:34.730
Wait, I can really have this?

09:34.730 --> 09:36.720
You had a quest out at sea?

09:36.720 --> 09:37.660
Yeah.

09:44.900 --> 09:47.210
Thank you! I'll take good care of it!

09:47.210 --> 09:49.300
I promise I won't lose it.

09:49.690 --> 09:50.610
I see.

10:02.150 --> 10:03.810
I've come.

10:10.130 --> 10:11.210
Goblins?

10:11.210 --> 10:13.700
Yes. Please help...

10:14.350 --> 10:15.300
No...

10:16.040 --> 10:18.410
Will you slay them?

10:18.930 --> 10:20.080
Of course.

10:24.600 --> 10:28.470
She takes care of me. 
She is also my bodyguard...

10:28.470 --> 10:30.790
though I told her that was unnecessary.

10:30.790 --> 10:35.570
You are quite skilled, but it's 
always dangerous to leave you alone.

10:35.570 --> 10:37.130
I have no other choice.

10:37.130 --> 10:38.340
Ugh.

10:38.340 --> 10:39.740
Ahem...

10:39.740 --> 10:42.140
So the goblins have been appearing...

10:42.140 --> 10:47.500
on this highway, from here, Water Town, 
through this town, and into the capital.

10:47.500 --> 10:49.070
A highway...

10:49.070 --> 10:52.310
I'm just so... so terrified...

10:52.760 --> 10:55.880
I just... can't go through.

10:56.140 --> 10:59.970
How many? Any nests? 
Any other information on the goblins?

10:59.970 --> 11:03.620
According to eyewitness accounts 
we've heard, there are around twenty.

11:03.620 --> 11:07.390
They all have matching tattoos. 
I haven't heard anything about their nests.

11:08.460 --> 11:10.850
They ride wolves.

11:11.150 --> 11:12.310
I see.

11:12.730 --> 11:18.470
The archbishop must participate in the 
meeting that will be held in the capital.

11:18.920 --> 11:21.290
That's why this request isn't 
specifically to slay the goblins,

11:21.290 --> 11:23.670
but to act as her bodyguard.

11:23.670 --> 11:26.960
They're probably wanderers without a nest.

11:27.290 --> 11:31.020
A wandering tribe. If I just kill 
them all when we run into them,

11:31.020 --> 11:32.040
it'll all be over.

11:32.330 --> 11:38.000
I believe that any other adventurer would 
do since we're just dealing with goblins...

11:38.240 --> 11:43.810
But the archbishop absolutely insists 
that it be you who accompanies her.

11:43.810 --> 11:47.180
Well, he's the most trustworthy 
gentleman that I know.

11:47.480 --> 11:50.960
I'm going to call... my comrades. 
Wait a while.

11:53.320 --> 11:56.330
The reward is a bag of gold, 
and it will be paid up front.

11:56.330 --> 11:58.920
Once we get to our destination, 
you will get another bag.

11:58.920 --> 12:04.820
Not bad. Taking a long journey to 
admire the capital might be all right.

12:04.820 --> 12:08.790
R-Right... The capital... The capital, huh?

12:08.790 --> 12:12.050
I guess I did want to go there at least once.

12:14.640 --> 12:15.680
Stop the carriage.

12:15.680 --> 12:17.370
As you command.

12:17.770 --> 12:18.870
Wait a moment.

12:25.160 --> 12:27.800
Beard-cutter sure is diligent.

12:34.060 --> 12:34.970
Pardon.

12:35.810 --> 12:36.850
Yes?

12:36.850 --> 12:40.230
Um... Who is he talking to?

12:40.550 --> 12:45.290
Um... The farm girl who 
Goblin Slayer lives with.

12:45.720 --> 12:46.750
I see.

12:50.760 --> 12:51.620
I'm done.

12:51.620 --> 12:53.160
Oh, right!

12:53.160 --> 12:56.080
Then let us continue on our way.

13:14.970 --> 13:16.320
Good evening.

13:17.430 --> 13:18.690
You're not going to sleep?

13:19.280 --> 13:25.150
I've been able to sleep well since the 
incident, so I wanted to thank you...

13:25.150 --> 13:26.660
But you're clearly awake.

13:26.660 --> 13:28.000
That's just because—

13:29.510 --> 13:32.050
You're so mean.

13:32.050 --> 13:32.950
I am?

13:33.510 --> 13:35.860
Goblins didn't appear.

13:36.200 --> 13:39.510
This carriage is being guarded 
by a group that's armed.

13:39.910 --> 13:41.820
It'd be too much trouble for 
them to attack up-front.

13:43.300 --> 13:45.460
They'll probably try tonight 
or tomorrow morning.

13:51.520 --> 13:52.290
Sleep.

13:53.030 --> 13:55.390
Close your eyes, and once you 
open them, it'll be morning.

13:58.490 --> 14:01.020
You make it sound so easy.

14:01.480 --> 14:03.250
I know that it's difficult.

14:04.140 --> 14:08.050
When I was a child, I tried to see 
how long I needed to close my eyes

14:08.050 --> 14:10.150
in bed before it became morning.

14:28.660 --> 14:33.430
Lady Archbishop? And Goblin Slayer?

14:33.430 --> 14:37.060
Um... Is something the matter?

14:37.590 --> 14:38.680
She woke up.

14:39.500 --> 14:42.770
I'd appreciate it if you didn't 
make me sound like some child!

14:45.190 --> 14:46.400
What?

14:46.810 --> 14:49.290
I just had trouble sleeping, that's all.

14:49.760 --> 14:51.870
Is everything all right with you?

14:51.870 --> 14:54.970
I just got a little thirsty, 
so I was getting some water.

14:55.330 --> 14:56.540
I see.

15:08.730 --> 15:10.930
I'll go wake everyone up.

15:13.510 --> 15:14.600
Don't let them notice you.

15:14.600 --> 15:15.500
I won't.

15:21.260 --> 15:22.350
Return to the carriage.

15:22.350 --> 15:23.040
Huh?

15:24.000 --> 15:24.910
Its dangerous.

15:27.520 --> 15:29.150
Lock the door and wait.

15:35.500 --> 15:38.060
All right. I'll be waiting for you.

15:40.770 --> 15:42.540
Is something the matter?

15:44.130 --> 15:45.790
Goblins have arrived.

15:48.810 --> 15:52.760
Please... don't let them get away alive.

16:21.140 --> 16:21.910
Tch.

16:27.070 --> 16:28.170
That's two.

16:28.530 --> 16:30.710
Don't let them escape. Kill them all.

16:33.880 --> 16:38.760
I see. No wonder carriages and such don't 
stand a chance when they're attacked.

16:38.760 --> 16:40.730
Get over here! It's dangerous!

16:40.730 --> 16:42.670
Oh, right. I'm sorry.

16:42.990 --> 16:46.380
I think we might be better off 
with slings than with miracles.

16:46.380 --> 16:51.070
Right. If you use Holy Light, 
this lot'll probably go running off.

16:58.630 --> 16:59.580
That's twelve.

16:59.580 --> 17:03.250
Being on the defensive doesn't 
seem to suit me well.

17:03.530 --> 17:05.920
Agreed. Can you move around them?

17:05.920 --> 17:10.820
I do not believe that "cannot" 
is in our vocabulary.

17:10.820 --> 17:13.180
I will be taking my leave.

17:17.110 --> 17:18.880
Goblin Slayer!

17:18.880 --> 17:20.430
We're going to make an anvil.

17:21.010 --> 17:22.010
Huh?

17:22.010 --> 17:22.810
What?!

17:22.810 --> 17:24.400
Hey, listen here, Orcbolg!

17:24.400 --> 17:26.760
We're going to strengthen our guard. 
Hurry and use Protection.

17:26.760 --> 17:28.100
Oh, r-right.

17:28.100 --> 17:29.830
You guard the other side.

17:29.830 --> 17:31.200
I'll handle things here.

17:31.200 --> 17:34.650
You got it... 
But I shouldn't be on the front lines.

17:34.920 --> 17:37.780
You're really pissing me off!

17:38.570 --> 17:40.510
You'd better apologize to me later!

17:40.510 --> 17:41.620
I don't follow.

17:41.620 --> 17:43.690
O merciful Earth Mother,

17:43.690 --> 17:47.550
please protect us, the weak, 
with the powers of the earth.

18:06.910 --> 18:08.060
Ah, I see.

18:08.310 --> 18:10.690
A hammer and anvil.

18:13.480 --> 18:16.070
Are we just going to surround 
them and crush them?

18:16.390 --> 18:17.780
Exactly.

18:18.140 --> 18:19.960
We're going to slay all of the goblins.

18:26.040 --> 18:27.060
Are you done?

18:27.510 --> 18:28.830
Y-Yes.

18:29.930 --> 18:30.920
How many?

18:31.760 --> 18:33.530
How many did these goblins get?

18:33.530 --> 18:34.550
Um...

18:35.500 --> 18:39.010
I believe I remember hearing 
it was a group of five or six.

18:39.010 --> 18:41.400
I see. Shut the window.

18:46.930 --> 18:49.390
Ew... Uh, what are you doing?

18:49.390 --> 18:50.640
I'm going to check.

18:51.530 --> 18:54.200
Sir Goblin Slayer, I will assist you.

18:54.200 --> 18:54.970
Thanks.

19:02.250 --> 19:03.630
We're missing some.

19:04.550 --> 19:05.240
What do you think?

19:05.240 --> 19:08.100
The likelihood that they're 
keeping them somewhere else...

19:08.100 --> 19:09.830
is probably low.

19:09.830 --> 19:12.130
Yeah. They're a wandering tribe.

19:12.130 --> 19:14.330
They should be wandering 
around with their captives.

19:14.330 --> 19:15.720
Which must mean...

19:16.040 --> 19:18.920
...that there are even more of them?

19:30.130 --> 19:31.570
This is amazing.

19:31.570 --> 19:33.980
This place is probably older than I am.

19:33.980 --> 19:37.460
You must really like it up there, huh?

19:37.460 --> 19:40.370
Well, we need to be on 
guard in all directions.

19:40.370 --> 19:42.080
Right, Orcbolg?

19:42.080 --> 19:42.660
Yeah.

19:44.120 --> 19:47.330
Ugh... Why'd you rip that off of them?

19:47.590 --> 19:52.340
There might be remnants or even 
commanders left of this tribe.

19:52.340 --> 19:55.080
It looks like a hand, 
but I'm not completely sure.

19:56.770 --> 19:57.690
You'll be left behind.

19:58.670 --> 20:01.090
I-I know!

20:01.090 --> 20:02.720
I know, okay?

20:06.300 --> 20:08.320
Welp...

20:08.320 --> 20:10.980
This is gonna take a while.

20:21.690 --> 20:24.820
I guess that's why it's taking so long.

20:24.820 --> 20:27.330
The king must've been 
absent from the capital.

20:27.330 --> 20:28.810
I wonder if something happened.

20:28.810 --> 20:29.540
Taxes.

20:29.800 --> 20:31.410
It's around the time they get collected.

20:31.410 --> 20:34.740
In places that don't have a governor 
or seem like an uprising may occur,

20:34.740 --> 20:36.300
the king appears personally.

20:36.300 --> 20:38.680
Huh... You seem pretty 
knowledgeable about this.

20:38.680 --> 20:39.960
I'm from a farming village.

20:43.320 --> 20:45.510
Halt. Present your identification.

20:48.690 --> 20:50.880
Now write your name and purpose here.

20:50.880 --> 20:52.390
Um, okay.

20:52.390 --> 20:53.480
Um...

20:53.480 --> 20:56.000
Would "bodyguard duty" suffice?

20:56.000 --> 20:58.170
If you're adventurers, yes.

20:58.170 --> 21:01.360
I see there's also a dwarf, 
an elf, and a lizardman.

21:01.360 --> 21:02.560
This goes for you, as well.

21:02.870 --> 21:04.400
And who are you?

21:04.850 --> 21:06.110
An adventurer.

21:08.340 --> 21:09.700
Silver-ranked?

21:09.990 --> 21:11.590
This had better not be a fake.

21:11.590 --> 21:13.010
The guild acknowledges me.

21:13.010 --> 21:15.330
In the name of the Supreme God...

21:16.420 --> 21:20.380
I vouch that he is indeed 
a silver-ranked adventurer.

21:20.380 --> 21:22.510
L-Lady Archbishop!

21:22.510 --> 21:24.540
I-I beg your pardon.

21:24.540 --> 21:26.010
Please go through.

21:26.010 --> 21:27.970
Paperwork is paperwork.

21:28.480 --> 21:30.930
Would you mind handing me the ledger, as well?

21:30.930 --> 21:32.800
Y-Yes, ma'am! Right away!

21:32.800 --> 21:34.560
Come on, you! Hurry up and write!

21:34.560 --> 21:35.250
All right.

21:43.630 --> 21:45.800
This is my first time here.

21:45.800 --> 21:47.840
Is it yours as well, Goblin Slayer?

21:47.840 --> 21:48.990
It is.

21:49.680 --> 21:52.690
I wish I could've brought my sister here.

21:54.350 --> 21:57.370
You may get a similar opportunity someday.

21:57.950 --> 21:59.100
I hope so.

23:32.010 --> 23:40.250
<b>Next Time</b>

23:32.010 --> 23:40.250
<b>City Adventure</b>
